# Every image is built from the repository root (apps/<name>/Dockerfile). The build installs and
# builds inside the image, so nothing a workstation installed, built or keeps locally belongs in
# the context: node_modules are symlinks into this checkout's store, and .env files hold real keys
# (a `node --env-file-if-exists=.env` start would silently pick one up from a layer).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.data
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.git
.nx
.husky/_
coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Generated by each app's build (Paraglide, Tailwind); regenerated inside the image.
apps/*/src/paraglide
apps/*/public/assets/app.css
apps/*/project.inlang/cache
# Next.js build output (apps/cms): its standalone tree carries a copy of the local .env.
**/.next
# apps/cms local uploads (the estate stores media in object storage).
apps/cms/media
